v_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":77.9,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.027078741388243788,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":6,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":66.7,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.0048926149258918805,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":42.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.1118270307328566,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":80.9,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.04842607634901396,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":64.9,"_gate_share_shrink":0.037638875934731475,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":3.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.015388628064684403,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":74.4,"_gate_insider_own":0.0018099999,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":1.2,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"S&P Global Inc., together with its subsidiaries, provides benchmarks, data, analytics, and workflow solutions in the global capital, energy and commodity, and automotive markets. It operates through four segments: S&P Global Market Intelligence, S&P Global Ratings, S&P Global Energy, and S&P Dow Jones Indices. The S&P Global Market Intelligence segment provides multi-asset-class data and analytics integrated with purpose-built workflow solutions. This segment offers Data, Analytics & Insights, a desktop product suite that provides data, analytics, and third-party research for global finance and corporate professionals; research, reference data, market data, derived analytics, and valuation services; enterprise solutions, such as software and workflow solutions; and credit and risk solutions for selling Ratings' credit ratings and related data and research, analytics, and financial risk solutions. The S&P Global Ratings segment operates as an independent provider of credit ratings, research, and analytics offering investors information and independent benchmarks for their investment and financial decisions as well as access to the capital markets. The S&P Global Energy segment provides information and benchmark prices for the energy and commodity markets. The S&P Dow Jones Indices segment operates as an index provider that maintains various valuation and index benchmarks for investment advisors, wealth managers, and institutional investors. It has operations in the United States, European region, Asia, and internationally. S&P Global Inc. was founded in 1860 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Catherine R. Clay | Chief Executive Officer of S&P Dow Jones Indices | Age 58","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 44K people. Revenue per employee of $345K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $123K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10). Recent headlines include layoff or workforce-reduction announcements.","financial_summary":["S&P Global Inc. is a large-cap financial services business with a $127.4B market cap on $15.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +23% over the past three years and +11% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $5.5B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 36 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.26\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 23\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 4.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 66% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6575952751959093},{"text":"Goodwill represents 60% of total assets \u2014 a large impairment risk hanging over book value","sev":"red","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Recent layoff news \u2014 often the market\u2019s first signal that growth is under pressure or costs are being rebased","sev":"amber","cat":"news"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Broad market in a downtrend, trading below its 200-day average","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Multiple macro indicators signal economic contraction","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 13% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Large open-market insider purchases (net $2.6M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","40 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is S&P Global (NYSE:SPGI) Building A Stronger Dividend Story?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/bluechip/is-sp-global-nysespgi-building-a-stronger-dividend-story","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795206720.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"S&P Global to Present at Goldman Sachs Financial Services Conference on December 8, 2026","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/sp-global-to-present-at-goldman-sachs-financial-services-conference-on-december-8-2026-302947341.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795210200.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"S&P Global to Present at UBS Global Technology and AI Conference on December 2, 2026","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/ai/articles/p-global-present-ubs-global-213000259.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795210200.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.637,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Surgery Partners, Inc. Announces Expiration and Results of Consent Solicitation Relating to Surgery Center Holdings, Inc.\u2019s 